    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d248">

                <pb facs="0536" n="514" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v16/pg514"/>

                <head>248. National Security Action Memorandum No. 71<anchor n="0" xml:id="d248-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1961-08-23">August 23,
                        1961</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list type="description">
                    <label>MEMORANDUM FOR</label>
                    <item>The Secretary of State</item>
                </list>
                <p>Having read the Department’s status report on the Cyprus situation,<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d248-f2"/> I am concerned over its gloomy tone. The inadequacies of
                    the Makarios government, as contrasted
                    with the discipline, energy, and able leadership of the local Communist Party,
                    are most worrisome.</p>
                <p>Perhaps we need some preventive medicine here to forestall further deterioration
                    of this situation. Shouldn’t we at a minimum push the UK, Greece, and Turkey to take a more forthcoming approach?
                    Moreover, in view of their limited resources, we should carefully review our own
                    policy of relying on these guarantor powers to shoulder the principal share of
                    the Western burden.</p>
                <p>Since Cyprus’ real estate and strategic location are of considerable importance
                    to us and to our allies, I would be grateful if the Department of State would
                    advise me on what measures would best insure our holding on to it, including
                    whatever use of US resources may be required.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">John F.
                                Kennedy</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d248-f1" n="0" type="source" xml:id="d248-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, S/S–NSC Files: Lot 72 D 316, NSAM 71. Secret.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d248-f2" n="1" xml:id="d248-f2-content">
                <p>The “Status Report on Cyprus,” August 18, outlined the state of political and
                    economic development in Cyprus during its first year of independence.
                    (Ibid.)</p>
            </note>
